# Citation File Format — https://citation-file-format.github.io
#
# rust-MAFFT is a pure-Rust port of MAFFT, the multiple sequence
# alignment software developed by Kazutaka Katoh and colleagues at the
# Computational Biology Research Center (CBRC). The scientific
# contribution — the FFT-anchored alignment algorithm, the iterative-
# refinement variants, the scoring matrices — is theirs. This port
# re-engineers that work in Rust while preserving byte-identical
# output.
#
# If you use rust-MAFFT in published work you MUST cite the original
# MAFFT paper (Katoh & Standley 2013, doi:10.1093/molbev/mst010). The
# rust-MAFFT manuscript (Goiriz, in preparation, Bioinformatics)
# describes the port and should be cited alongside once published.
# Full citation guidance at:
#     https://luksgrin.github.io/rust-MAFFT/citation/
#
# NB: This file is deliberately minimal to satisfy Zenodo's cffconvert
# pipeline (which has historically been strict about license-as-list,
# nested publisher entities, and preferred-citation blocks). Mode-
# specific references and BibTeX entries live in docs/citation.md.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use rust-MAFFT in scientific work, please cite the original
  MAFFT paper: Katoh K, Standley DM (2013) MAFFT multiple sequence
  alignment software version 7: improvements in performance and
  usability. Molecular Biology and Evolution 30(4):772-780.
  doi:10.1093/molbev/mst010. The scientific contribution is theirs;
  this work is a Rust port. See https://luksgrin.github.io/rust-MAFFT/citation/
  for the full citation guide.
title: rust-MAFFT
abstract: >-
  Pure-Rust port of MAFFT 7.526 producing byte-identical output across
  the BAliBASE 3 benchmark (1930/1930) for every supported alignment
  mode. Distributed as a Rust library (mafft, mafft-core), a standalone
  CLI (mafft-rs), and Python bindings (pymafft).
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Goiriz
    given-names: Lucas
    email: lucas.goiriz@csic.es
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-09-06"
# SPDX identifier (Zenodo's cffconvert rejects expressions like
# "MIT AND BSD-3-Clause" — keep this a single SPDX ID for compat).
# The BSD-3-Clause covers the algorithmic constructs ported from
# upstream MAFFT; see LICENSE-BSD in the repo root.
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/luksgrin/rust-MAFFT"
url: "https://luksgrin.github.io/rust-MAFFT/"
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - multiple-sequence-alignment
  - msa
  - mafft
  - rust
  - port
